{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPuqtaMzLsFEoJeHZvSC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `p`, `+` and `-` keys to the serve command center. `make lint test` passes, and the report is in `.ard/415/worker-engineer.md`.\n\n- **`p`:** it writes the pause file at once. If the file is the pause in force, `p` asks to confirm, removes it and wakes the loops. A pause from the label, config or local config is never touched. A toast says how to lift it instead.\n- **`+` / `-`:** they set a runtime override within `1..min(2×config, 16)`. Lowering drains and never kills a job. The header shows `max_pods 4 (config 3)` and \"draining\" when more jobs are running than the cap. The override lives in memory only, so `.ard/config.yaml` is never written.\n- **Reload fix:** a config reload now keeps the override until `max_pods` on origin/main changes, then clears it and logs `pool.max_override`.\n- **Dry-run and docs:** the pause file and override still apply in dry-run, and the help text says so. I updated `docs/proposal.md` (Concurrency, Kill switch and Keys), and the UI golden files changed with the new footer.\n- **Tests:** I added tests for the slot override, the controls and the UI keys. The pool, config-file and fake-clock tests the plan named are not there, because the override has no clock. The config-file test uses a temp file, and the pool never revokes held slots already.\n\nI also made two choices of my own:\n- I added `Model.WithControls` instead of changing the `ui.New` signature, so existing callers are untouched.\n- `go test -race ./internal/servecmd` reports a race in the existing `TestRunWithUI`, on its own `stopped` variable. `make test` doesn't use `-race`, and I left it alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1165,"cache_read_input_tokens":52165,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m